#edb/ref 17592186166935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049381 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049381 #edb/ref 1033 3190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049381 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "f0242aed-46fd-5f2e-bcc2-49ee070cdccf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049896 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049896 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049896 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049896 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049896 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049896 #edb/ref 1033 3232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049896 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "1c8e94f0-f686-5ab0-b88e-99e6f26eaf54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428581 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428582 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs With Distinct Eigenvalues and Initial Conditions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1033 2088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "2d131eff-4143-5f33-ab1b-d2795c01303f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050768 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050768 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050768 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186147512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050768 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186147513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050768 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186147514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050768 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186147515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050768 #edb/ref 1031 "Inverse Laplace Transforms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050768 #edb/ref 1033 2530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050768 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "65390005-2dba-5f37-a0b9-caa26be8d127" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164006 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164006 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164006 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164006 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164006 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "04e2a43b-dabf-5ab6-81ef-f416beb9dc57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164007 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164007 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164007 #edb/ref 1077 "field-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164007 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164007 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "146c7af2-ba63-5e52-a59f-53646c3ff217" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164008 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164008 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164008 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164008 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164008 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "34e53997-6284-545e-90f3-20254b9df98a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164009 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164009 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164009 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186164009 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7c6ef50d-1297-553c-9b69-f8165c2b7fcf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166508 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21155" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166508 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/28/287223863402ec50768dee1bf0910226fbb0f9ee4818faaae4a0f1bd6121df26.svg)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$ \nFind the solution of the new system in terms of the parameter $s.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166508 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d9715a0c-6808-5db8-b0b4-5bedc4f2e9e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166508 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\,\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\,\\{-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\,\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\,\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\,\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L\\,\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\,\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\,\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L\\,\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-L\\,\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ -3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1){X}_{2}(s)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the first equation, we have\n\n$$\nX_2(s) = (s+3)X_1(s) - 4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1)\\,[(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4] & =4 \\\\ -3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1)(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4(s+1) & =4 \\\\ [(s+1)(s+3)-3]{X}_{1}(s) & =4+4(s+1) \\\\ s(s+4){X}_{1}(s) & =4s+8 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $X_2(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{2}(s) & =(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4 \\\\  & =(s+3)\\,(\\frac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)})-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4(s+3)(s+2)-4s(s+4)}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4({s}^{2}+5s+6)-4({s}^{2}+4s)}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}+20s+24-4{s}^{2}-16s}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(s+6)}{s(s+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nX_1(s) =\\dfrac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)}, \n\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{4(s+6)}{s(s+4)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166509 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21156" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166509 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/8d/8da4fe8a52643867946a0818f3181fa57d6dc5b067155876e26689cb3fdde85e.svg)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ x_1(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{4}{s} + \\dfrac{1}{s-6}, \n\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ x_2(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{20}{s} - \\dfrac{1}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166509 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ec8e6fde-504e-581f-b465-6a9bc3927d77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166509 #edb/ref 1074 "To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{20}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =20{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =20\\cdot 1-{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =20-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ 20-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166510 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21157" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166510 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/3f/3fa8db8d4186569020d5805ac76eee4f92f1c261dd2acb2502409a9b2b6db56b.svg)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXX}[/math]}}=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ \\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXX}[/math]}}=\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXXXXXXX}[/math]}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166510 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0b2a74d8-1ce2-5055-a843-1456b1878cf7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166510 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-3{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{9{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=9L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-7=9{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186390939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186390955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166930 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "fd7b8fc8-26d3-5551-9a46-45725bd863a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166931 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166931 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166931 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166931 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166931 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166931 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166931 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 175921863