#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1050 1080.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "18df0fdd-60be-5a81-a0cd-e95103dfb1c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167160 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186164006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167160 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186164007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167160 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186164008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167160 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186164009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167160 #edb/ref 1069 "q-322288" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167160 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167160 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{7/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167160 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5075353c-c362-57ce-9a2a-4c2ae80aa981" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167160 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{7/2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-\\frac{7}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{1\\cdot t}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1/2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7/2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167163 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167163 #edb/ref 1069 "q-322291" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167163 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167163 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167163 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "352d1492-cbac-52be-ab13-b4b1c7ef68ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167163 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-9={X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-6=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)=9 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-2){X}_{2}(s)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s)]+2{X}_{2}(s) & =9 \\\\ 6(s-1)-[(s-1)(s-2)-2]{X}_{2}(s) & =9 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-3s){X}_{2}(s) & =9-6(s-1) \\\\ -s(s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =-6s+15 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =6-(s-2)\\cdot \\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6s(s-3)-3(s-2)(2s-5)}{s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(3s-10)}{s(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(3s-10)}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167886 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167886 #edb/ref 1061 590676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167886 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "648d1a99-8c25-5200-8b95-382792dca052" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167886 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167887 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167887 #edb/ref 1061 590677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167887 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "887d1a2a-3793-57e6-a390-bcc123897754" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167887 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167888 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167888 #edb/ref 1061 590680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167888 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c39529f2-6303-5dd8-a113-cdaf40a5d673" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167888 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167889 #edb/ref 1061 590683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167889 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aa736c0f-1eaa-5601-a02e-62159a1f73b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167889 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167890 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167890 #edb/ref 1061 590687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167890 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f663bde1-a39c-5d4d-83fd-15b833a5cbea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167890 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167982 #edb/ref 1064 "![](images/44/44a90d0fa61d3643848f01479706cca752a00914b99185da5b8739c5e1cab182.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. In the initial value problem above, we apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation.\n\nFirst, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{5{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=5L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+6L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3=5{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+6{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$\n\n**Step 2**. Now, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns X_1(s) +  3 = 5 X_1(s)\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_1(s) = -\\dfrac{3}{s-5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns X_2(s) -  2 = -2\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{s-5}\\right) + 6 X_2(s) \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**. To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{3}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{8}{s-6}-\\frac{6}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\}-6{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ 8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167982 #edb/ref 1065 14201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167982 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a475ed27-9529-52d2-85cb-9e8827c5b45e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167982 #edb/ref 1067 "A Worked Example" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168031 #edb/ref 1064 "In this topic, we'll learn how to use Laplace transforms to solve homogeneous systems like the one below.\n![](images/66/66eb9ce1b87b67ba550fc0b76493b775bf2b2e67be257b9fe9974db9d53cdffa.svg)\n\nThe process can be split into three steps.\n\n- **Step 1.** Apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation, to get a system with variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Solve the obtained system for variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** To find the initial variables\n\n$$\nx_1(t) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad x_2(t)\n$$\n\nsatisfying the original initial value problem, apply the inverse Laplace transform to \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\nLet's see how this works in practice." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168031 #edb/ref 1065 14610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168031 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "98573e3a-ebcd-565e-8de7-a83e3deb9d09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168031 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301167 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3(3s-10)}{s(s-3)}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301167 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301167 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f40a260d-0b29-5e36-b2a9-5799775c5e4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301428 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186301167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301428 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301428 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301428 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186301167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301428 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3e2b49cd-92af-5da9-9339-22182fbb3716" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302528 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302528 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302528 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ad4202e-4528-57fc-b977-aa5764d